<section class="panel" aria-label="Grade 3 Unit 8 Lesson 5 room furnishing cost project">
<h2>Tiny House: Cost</h2>
<p><a href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-8/lesson-5/lesson.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original 2021 teacher source and labelled bus cost image</a>. Teacher must verify original cost sheet and photo; they are not copied or numerically transcribed here.</p>
<p>Start with too-low, about-right and too-high estimates for the labelled bus image, using actual source values with your teacher.</p>
<p>Use the tiny-house room YOU designed in Lesson 4. Choose finishing items and quantities from the teacher's original source cost sheet. The exact total must be <strong>at most $1,000</strong>. Make calculations item price × quantity, sum and subtract the remainder.</p>
<p>Independent arithmetic practice only, using newly invented figures, NOT publisher prices: $450 + $200 + $100 + $180 = $930 spent, leaving $70. Your authentic class results depend on the real source cost sheet.</p>
<p>Compare choices with a partner and revise an unaffordable plan. Explain the selected room, items and necessity of floor coverings or plumbing to your teacher. Publisher gated Cool-down is excluded.</p>
</section>
